{"id":"chatcmpl-40c763b9-4be3-4f6a-979d-5e879c0574df","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246590,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first approach to medical image interpretation: first obtain a domain-expert interpretation, then independently confirm the critical spatial attribute (laterality) using a grounding/localization tool before committing to an answer. The key insight is that laterality in radiology requires reconciling image-space coordinates with patient-side anatomy via orientation markers, not naive left/right assumptions.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on a single spatial attribute (side, location, extent), use a dedicated localization/grounding tool to independently confirm that attribute rather than relying solely on a holistic expert read.\",\n    \"Translate image-space coordinates into patient-side anatomy by checking for orientation markers (e.g., 'L'/'R' labels) before mapping to answer options.\",\n    \"Decompose the question into the discriminating attribute first (here: laterality), then verify only that attribute to avoid over-analysis.\",\n    \"Use a two-source confirmation strategy: one source for the finding's presence/identity, a second for its spatial verification, and only answer when they agree.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Always resolve laterality via orientation markers; treat image-left/right as distinct from patient-left/right. Confirm the finding's identity and its side with separate evidence.\",\n    \"Spatial attribute questions\": \"Identify the single discriminating attribute, then use a grounding/localization tool to confirm it with coordinates before selecting an option.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification\": \"Pair a domain-expert tool (holistic judgment) with a grounding tool (precise localization); require agreement before finalizing the answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm orientation: locate any side markers (L/R) and map image coordinates to patient anatomy before choosing left vs. right.\",\n    \"Cross-check: ensure the expert interpretation and the grounded localization agree on the discriminating attribute before answering.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":463,"total_tokens":865,"completion_tokens":402,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":463},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":402}}}